# Credentials for the Pipedream CLI (`pd`), used from this checkout.
#
# `pd init connect` writes the real `.env` beside this file. Copy this one and
# fill it in only if you need to run `pd` by hand — nothing in the app or the
# Edge Functions reads this file.
#
# The deployed functions get these as Supabase secrets, set per branch and never
# inherited from prod:
#
#   SUPABASE_ACCESS_TOKEN=sbp_… supabase secrets set \
#     --project-ref <ref> PIPEDREAM_CLIENT_ID=…
#
# Background: supabase/integrations/README.md. `.env` is gitignored; keep it
# that way.

# Credentials for calling *Pipedream's own* API — not a connected product's.
# Minted with `pd oauth-client create <name>`, which is a different thing from
# the per-app custom OAuth clients that carry Slack's or Linear's own
# client_id/secret (those are configured in the Connect UI, never here).
PIPEDREAM_CLIENT_ID=REPLACE_ME
PIPEDREAM_CLIENT_SECRET=REPLACE_ME

# Which Connect environment every call is tagged with, and it is not a label.
# `development` is capped at 10 external users and requires each of them to be
# signed in to pipedream.com — our own testing only. Production has to be
# `production`, which is enabled on Pipedream's pricing page.
PIPEDREAM_ENVIRONMENT=development

# The Connect project the external users hang off. Connect → Settings.
PIPEDREAM_PROJECT_ID=REPLACE_ME

# Written by the `pd` scaffold for its own chat sample. Nothing in this
# repository reads it; left here so a copied `.env` matches what the CLI writes
# rather than looking half-filled.
AUTH_SECRET=REPLACE_ME
